{"step_index":344,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T08:23:43Z","content":"Both root causes have been surgically fixed:\n\n### Fix 1: Orbit Lines Locked to Satellites (`PathGraphics`)\n- **Removed** the static `trailPositions[]` array and the `polyline` property entirely. Static polyline coordinate arrays are baked in ECEF at initialization time — when Cesium's clock advances and the globe rotates, the satellite's `SampledPositionProperty` correctly interpolates to the new ECEF position, but the static polyline stays frozen in its original frame, causing the visual drift.\n- **Replaced** it with `Cesium.PathGraphics` attached directly to the entity. `PathGraphics` natively reads from `entity.position` at every frame, drawing a glowing trail 60 minutes ahead (`leadTime: 3600`) and 60 minutes behind (`trailTime: 3600`). The satellite is now **mathematically welded** to its orbital track. Debris gets a red glow, active satellites get cyan.\n\n### Fix 2: TCA Zoom Blackout (`flyToBoundingSphere`)\n- **Root cause**: The two conjunction objects are only ~1.2 km apart. The old `camera.flyTo` with a destination offset tried to frame a near-zero bounding box, collapsing the camera frustum to nothing → black screen.\n- **Fix**: Replaced with `viewer.camera.flyToBoundingSphere()` using a `BoundingSphere` with a **150 km bounding radius** centered on the midpoint between both objects. The `HeadingPitchRange` offset enforces a hard **500 km viewing distance** at a **-35° downward pitch**, guaranteeing the camera always parks at a safe, cinematic vantage point with the 4K Earth visible in the background. The `viewer.trackedEntity` is explicitly cleared first to prevent the tracking system from overriding the safe distance.\n\n**Please refresh your browser at http://localhost:3000**. On the 3D tab, confirm that STARLINK-1007 rides directly on its glowing orbital trail, then click **⚠ JUMP TO TCA** to verify the camera glides to a beautifully framed 500 km vantage point without any black screen!"}
{"step_index":345,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T08:27:44Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n\"We are adding an enterprise feature: a 1-Click Official Conjunction Assessment Report (PDF Export) that generates an executive, aerospace-grade flight safety brief.Please update index.html and app.js with the following:Library Import (index.html):Add the lightweight PDF generation library: <script src=\"[https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jspdf/2.5.1/jspdf.umd.min.js](https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jspdf/2.5.1/jspdf.umd.min.js)\"></script>.Export UI Button:Add a sleek [ ⤓ EXPORT AUDIT REPORT ] button with glassmorphism styling (border border-cyan-500/40 hover:bg-cyan-500/20 text-cyan-400 font-mono text-xs px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg transition-all flex items-center gap-1.5) in two places:In the main top-right header next to 'REFRESH LIVE DATA'.Inside the CAM Planner drawer right next to 'AUTHORIZE MANEUVER'.Dynamic PDF Construction (app.js):Write a function generateConjunctionReport(eventData) using jspdf.Layout specifications:Theme: Dark/clean professional layout (monochrome slate with subtle cyan accent lines).Header: 'ORBITAL GUARD // CONJUNCTION ASSESSMENT REPORT (CAR)' with a generated Document ID (e.g., CAR-2026-09-8842), classification badge [ UNCLASSIFIED / OPERATIONAL BRIEF ], and generation timestamp (UTC).Section 1: Event Summary Table: Primary Object, Secondary Object, NORAD IDs, Time of Closest Approach (UTC), Miss Distance ($d$), and Calculated Collision Probability ($P_c$).Section 2: Risk Assessment: Risk classification badge (CRITICAL, MODERATE, or NOMINAL) along with regulatory threshold compliance statement ($P_c > 1.0\\times 10^{-4}$ actionable threshold).Section 3: Recommended Collision Avoidance Maneuver (CAM): If generated from the CAM drawer, include the planned In-Track $\\Delta v$, propulsion type (Chemical vs. Electric), propellant mass penalty (kg), and post-maneuver estimated miss distance.Footer: Formal verification notice: 'Propagated via SGP4 analytical theory & 2D Gaussian B-Plane integral. Certified for Space Situational Awareness (SSA) flight dynamics handoff.'Automatically trigger the browser download named OrbitalGuard_CAR_<EventID>.pdf.Action: Implement the PDF generation code, trigger a test download from the CAM drawer for the critical conjunction event, and verify the formatted PDF downloads cleanly.\"\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-27T13:57:44+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":346,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T08:27:44Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 5 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. \"The 3D orbit viewer is blacking out and blurring when zooming into a satellite because the camera is clipping through the entity and looking into empty space. We also need to add more technical realism to the CAM Planner.Please update app.js and index.html with the following:1. Fix the 3D Cinematic Camera (No More Black Screens):When a user double-clicks an entity (or clicks it in the table), use viewer.flyTo(entity, { offset: new Cesium.HeadingPitchRange(0, -Cesium.Math.toRadians(30), 50000) }). This stops the camera 50 km away and tilts it 30 degrees down so the 4K Earth is always in the cinematic background.Upgrade the satellite graphics: Instead of the default blurry Cesium.PointGraphics, use Cesium.BillboardGraphics. Set the image to a glowing target reticle SVG (you can generate a data URI for a clean, futuristic circle with a dot in the middle).2. Upgrade the CAM Planner Functionality:Propulsion System Selector: In the CAM Drawer, add a dropdown or toggle for 'Propulsion Type' with two options: 'Ch\n<truncated 998 bytes>\n2. \"The 3D globe is glitching when I try to move it! The auto-rotate is fighting my mouse, the trackpad inertia is too slippery, and the camera is still clipping (blacking out) when zooming in. Let's make this feel like a butter-smooth 120Hz native app.\n\nPlease update app.js with the following fixes:\n\n1. Butter-Smooth 120Hz Controls:\n\nSet viewer.targetFrameRate = 120; to uncap the rendering speed.\n\nFix the slippery trackpad by disabling inertia. Set viewer.scene.screenSpaceCameraController.inertiaSpin = 0;, inertiaTranslate = 0;, and inertiaZoom = 0;.\n\n2. Smart Auto-Rotate (Stop Glitching):\n\nDo not run rotateRight() blindly on every tick. Add a boolean flag let isInteracting = false;.\n\n\n<truncated 18541 bytes>\ns`) — lines 520-600\n  - CAM Drawer logic (TCA clock, propulsion, burn direction, Delta-v simulation, authorize) — lines 610-850\n  - **PENDING:** Need to add `generateConjunctionReport()` function and wire export buttons.\n\n- **`/Users/anandgopaltiwary/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/space_debris_prototype/backend/main.py`**: GET /api/tles, GET /api/conjunctions, POST /api/mission-risk.\n- **`/Users/anandgopaltiwary/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/space_debris_prototype/backend/sgp4_calc.py`**: SGP4 propagation, 2D Gaussian Pc, mock critical conjunction injection.\n\n### Running Background Tasks\n- Frontend server: `python3 -m http.server 3000` in `frontend/` dir (task-28, daemon)\n- Backend server: `uvicorn main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000` in `backend/` dir with venv activated (task-169, daemon)\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n**Immediately before this checkpoint:** The user requested the PDF export feature. No code has been written for it yet. Status: NOT STARTED.\n\n**Next steps — implement in this order:**\n\n1. **Add jspdf CDN** to `index.html` `<head>` section (after nipplejs import, around line 13):\n   ```html\n   <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jspdf/2.5.1/jspdf.umd.min.js\"></script>\n   ```\n\n2. **Add Export button in header** (next to the \"Refresh Live Data\" button, around line 86 in index.html).\n\n3. **Add Export button in CAM drawer** (next to \"Authorize Maneuver\" button, around line 220 in index.html).\n\n4. **Write `generateConjunctionReport(eventData)` in app.js** using `window.jspdf.jsPDF`. The function should:\n   - Generate Document ID: `CAR-${year}-${month}-${random4digit}`\n   - Build dark professional layout with header, 3 sections, and footer per the user's exact specifications\n   - Accept event data that includes: object names, TCA, miss distance, Pc, and optionally CAM data (delta-v, propulsion type, fuel cost, post-maneuver distance)\n   - Auto-d\n---\nThe checkpoint summary has been truncated due to hitting max length. Please see the conversation log file for the full conversation.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
